    {
      "title": "Retryable Writes",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Enabled by default since MongoDB 4.2. The driver automatically retries eligible write operations exactly once after a transient network error or a failover.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#retryable-writes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Eligible operations: insertOne, updateOne, replaceOne, deleteOne, findOneAndUpdate, findOneAndReplace, findOneAndDelete, insertMany (ordered or unordered), bulkWrite (ordered or unordered).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#retryable-writes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "updateMany, deleteMany (not idempotent at the protocol level)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#retryable-writes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Writes with w: 0 (unacknowledged)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#retryable-writes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Individual writes within an explicit transaction (the transaction itself is retried)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#retryable-writes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "RetryableWriteError - the driver retries automatically",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#retryable-writes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "NoWritesPerformed (MongoDB 6.1+) - both attempts failed without writing; safe to retry at app layer",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#retryable-writes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "TransientTransactionError - retry the entire transaction",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#retryable-writes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "UnknownTransactionCommitResult - retry commitTransaction()",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#retryable-writes",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Retryable Reads",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Enabled by default since MongoDB 4.2. The driver retries eligible read operations exactly once after transient network errors.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#retryable-reads",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Eligible operations: find, findOne, aggregate (without $out/$merge), distinct, count, estimatedDocumentCount, listDatabases, listCollections, listIndexes.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#retryable-reads",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Error Handling Strategy Checklist",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Let the driver handle retryable errors (retryWrites/retryReads).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#error-handling-strategy-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Catch DuplicateKeyError (11000) for idempotent upserts.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#error-handling-strategy-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Catch ServerSelectionTimeoutError for connectivity failures and alert.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#error-handling-strategy-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Catch WriteConcernError when w: majority cannot be satisfied.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#error-handling-strategy-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Catch MaxTimeMSExpired (50) and investigate slow queries.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#error-handling-strategy-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Wrap bulk operations to inspect BulkWriteError.writeErrors array.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#error-handling-strategy-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Log error codes, not just messages, for searchability.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#error-handling-strategy-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Never swallow errors silently; always log or propagate.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#error-handling-strategy-checklist",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "When to Use",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Use transactions when business logic requires atomic updates across multiple documents or collections.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#when-to-use",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Prefer single-document atomicity when possible; redesign schemas before reaching for transactions.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#when-to-use",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Transactions are supported on replica sets (4.0+) and sharded clusters (4.2+).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#when-to-use",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Transaction Retry Pattern",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Use withTransaction() (available in all drivers) instead of manual startTransaction()/commitTransaction(). The helper automatically retries on TransientTransactionError and retries commit on UnknownTransactionCommitResult.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#transaction-retry-pattern",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "If using manual control:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#transaction-retry-pattern",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Transaction Anti-Patterns",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Transactions lasting >5 seconds (increases WiredTiger cache pressure and conflict risk).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#transaction-anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Modifying >1,000 documents in a single transaction.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#transaction-anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Using transactions for single-document operations (unnecessary overhead).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#transaction-anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Not using withTransaction() helper (loses automatic retry logic).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#transaction-anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Running DDL inside transactions (createCollection, createIndex).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#transaction-anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Relying on transactions instead of redesigning schema for single-document atomicity.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#transaction-anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Client-Level Bulk Write (MongoDB 8.0+)",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "MongoDB 8.0 introduced client-level bulkWrite() that can write to multiple collections and databases in a single network round-trip:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#client-level-bulk-write-mongodb-80",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Bulk Operation Best Practices",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Use unordered for maximum throughput when order does not matter.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#bulk-operation-best-practices",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Batch sizes: the driver auto-batches into 100,000-operation groups. For very large imports, chunk at the application level.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#bulk-operation-best-practices",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Catch BulkWriteError and inspect writeErrors to identify which operations failed.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#bulk-operation-best-practices",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Use upsert: true in UpdateOne/ReplaceOne models for idempotent loads.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#bulk-operation-best-practices",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "For multi-million-row imports, use mongoimport or mongorestore instead of driver bulk writes.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#bulk-operation-best-practices",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Running Pipelines",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "All drivers support collection.aggregate(pipeline, options). Key options:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#running-pipelines",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Aggregation Best Practices",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Place $match and $project as early as possible to reduce documents flowing through the pipeline.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#aggregation-best-practices",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Use $match before $lookup to limit the join scope.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#aggregation-best-practices",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Set allowDiskUse: true only when necessary (large groupings/sorts).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#aggregation-best-practices",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Use maxTimeMS to prevent runaway pipelines.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#aggregation-best-practices",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Use $merge or $out for materialized views, not in-app aggregation.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#aggregation-best-practices",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Use explain('executionStats') to verify index utilization in $match stages.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#aggregation-best-practices",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Change Stream Best Practices",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Always persist resume tokens - store in a separate collection or external store for crash recovery.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#change-stream-best-practices",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Use fullDocument: 'updateLookup' when you need the complete document after an update.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#change-stream-best-practices",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Use fullDocumentBeforeChange: 'whenAvailable' (6.0+) for audit trails.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#change-stream-best-practices",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Filter early with $match in the pipeline to reduce network traffic.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#change-stream-best-practices",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Handle invalidate events (dropped collection, renamed collection) by reopening the stream.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#change-stream-best-practices",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "For cross-collection CDC, watch at the database level: db.watch().",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#change-stream-best-practices",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "For cluster-wide events, watch at the client level: client.watch().",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#change-stream-best-practices",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "When to Use",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Files larger than 16 MB BSON document limit.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#when-to-use-1",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Storing files alongside metadata in MongoDB without a separate file service.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#when-to-use-1",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Accessing portions of large files without loading the entire file into memory.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#when-to-use-1",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Keeping files synchronized across distributed deployments.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#when-to-use-1",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "How GridFS Works",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "GridFS stores each file as two sets of documents:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#how-gridfs-works",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "fs.files - metadata (filename, length, chunkSize, uploadDate, md5, contentType)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#how-gridfs-works",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "fs.chunks - binary data in 255 KB chunks (default), indexed by files_id + n",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#how-gridfs-works",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "GridFS Best Practices",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Use GridFS only for files >16 MB. For smaller files, store as BinData in documents.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#gridfs-best-practices",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Set appropriate chunkSizeBytes - smaller chunks for random-access reads, larger for sequential streaming.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#gridfs-best-practices",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Index fs.files on fields you query (e.g., metadata.author, filename).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#gridfs-best-practices",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Use streaming APIs (not readAll) to avoid loading entire files into memory.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#gridfs-best-practices",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Consider Atlas Data Lake or S3 for very large-scale file storage; GridFS is not a CDN replacement.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#gridfs-best-practices",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "mongosh Best Practices",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Use --file for repeatable scripts, not interactive copy-paste.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#mongosh-best-practices",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Use --quiet in CI/CD to suppress the mongosh banner.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#mongosh-best-practices",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Use printjson() for structured output; print() for plain text.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#mongosh-best-practices",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Store maintenance scripts in version control alongside application code.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#mongosh-best-practices",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Use --eval for one-liners in shell scripts and cron jobs.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#mongosh-best-practices",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "mongosh supports full ES2022+: use async/await, destructuring, for...of, and template literals.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#mongosh-best-practices",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Use .mongoshrc.js for custom prompts, helpers, and default config.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#mongosh-best-practices",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "14. Resilient Application Checklist",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Use this checklist when reviewing any application that connects to MongoDB:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#14-resilient-application-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[ ] Single client instance shared across the application",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#14-resilient-application-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[ ] Connection string uses SRV format for Atlas / DNS seedlist deployments",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#14-resilient-application-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[ ] appName set for observability",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#14-resilient-application-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[ ] retryWrites and retryReads enabled (default since 4.2)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#14-resilient-application-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[ ] Write concern set to majority for durability",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#14-resilient-application-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[ ] Read preference matches the use case (primary for consistency, secondary for read scale)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#14-resilient-application-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[ ] maxPoolSize right-sized for deployment environment",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#14-resilient-application-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[ ] serverSelectionTimeoutMS set to a reasonable value (not infinite)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#14-resilient-application-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[ ] Graceful shutdown closes the client",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#14-resilient-application-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[ ] Error handling catches specific error types, not generic exceptions",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#14-resilient-application-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[ ] Duplicate key errors handled for idempotent operations",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#14-resilient-application-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[ ] Transactions use withTransaction() helper with automatic retry",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#14-resilient-application-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[ ] Projections used to limit returned fields",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#14-resilient-application-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[ ] Indexes cover query patterns (ESR rule)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#14-resilient-application-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[ ] maxTimeMS set on long-running queries and aggregations",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#14-resilient-application-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[ ] Change stream resume tokens persisted for crash recovery",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#14-resilient-application-checklist",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[ ] Monitoring events wired to observability stack (pool events, command events, SDAM events)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/mongodb-developer/#14-resilient-application-checklist",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
